### how wide the over-claim is, for the one span where both sides are declared axes
  132's commutation span names, jointly:
    (deterministic rounding members) x {saturation}
    (translation-equivariant members) x {wrapping}
  Written per axis it becomes rounding: {det union transeq} x overflow_policy: {sat, wrap},
  which additionally claims the two cells (transeq, saturation) and (det, wrapping).
  The source claims neither. Two cells invented by the notation, silently, on a row
  whose Argument kind is equivariance.

